# Build context hygiene.
#
# The important line is /data and *.db. The data folder holds your SQLite database, your resumes,
# your verified profile and your encrypted API keys. Without these the whole thing gets copied into
# the build context, which means it lands in the daemon's cache — and in the image, if any layer is
# careless. A .dockerignore is the cheapest privacy control in this repo.

# Never ship user data into an image.
data/
data-*/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-journal
.env

# Build output: regenerated inside the image, and the host copy would fight it.
artifacts/
artifacts-*/
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
server/wwwroot/
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Repo furniture.
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
TestResults/
coverage/

# Docs are not needed at runtime. Kept out only to keep the context small.
progress.md